{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bifrost V1 - Virtual Key Quota",
    "description": "Wire-contract tests for the self-service quota endpoint GET /api/governance/virtual-keys/quota. The VK value in the header is the credential (no admin auth): x-bf-vk accepts any value, Authorization Bearer requires the sk-bf- prefix. Covers the response shape (budgets, rate_limit, provider_configs, model_configs), 401 on a missing header, 401 (not 404) on an unknown key, and usage visibility after an inference call. The quota endpoint reads the database, which trails the in-memory counters by up to the 10s dump ticker, so the usage check polls with a 30s ceiling. An expired key is rejected with 403 while an inactive one still reads its quota with is_active false. The rotation grace-window quota cases live in bifrost-v1-vk-rotation-cooldown (they need rotation state).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
